Vendored from npm, served at /assets/ (src/routes/mod.rs):

  htmx.min.js       htmx.org@2.0.11, dist/htmx.min.js
  htmx-ext-sse.js   htmx-ext-sse@2.2.4, dist/sse.js
  normalize.css     normalize.css@8.0.1, normalize.css
  photoswipe-lightbox.esm.min.js
                    photoswipe@5.4.4, dist/photoswipe-lightbox.esm.min.js
  photoswipe.esm.min.js
                    photoswipe@5.4.4, dist/photoswipe.esm.min.js
  photoswipe-LICENSE.txt
                    photoswipe@5.4.4, LICENSE (MIT)

  highlightjs/core.min.js       @highlightjs/cdn-assets@11.12.0, es/core.min.js
                                (served as /assets/highlightjs-core.min.js)
  highlightjs/languages/*.js    @highlightjs/cdn-assets@11.12.0, languages/*
                                (all 193, embedded by build.rs; bundled for
                                highlighted_languages at /highlight-js/...)
  highlightjs/LICENSE           @highlightjs/cdn-assets@11.12.0, LICENSE
                                (BSD-3-Clause)

highlight.js must stay at the version Discourse pins in
frontend/discourse/package.json (exactly 11.12.0): the bundle's digest
(HighlightJs.version) is a sha1 over these files, so another version gives
other urls than Rails'.

  floating-ui.core.umd.min.js @floating-ui/core@1.8.0, dist/floating-ui.core.umd.min.js
  floating-ui.dom.umd.min.js  @floating-ui/dom@1.8.0, dist/floating-ui.dom.umd.min.js

@floating-ui/dom is the version Discourse's pnpm-lock.yaml resolves for
float-kit (MIT, Copyright (c) 2021-present Floating UI contributors). The
UMD builds are plain scripts: core defines window.FloatingUICore (with
@floating-ui/utils inlined) and dom, loaded after it, window.FloatingUIDOM.

Each was checked against the package tarball's npm integrity (sha512) and
compared byte for byte with the file in the tarball. To update, fetch the
new versions the same way and check them again:

  curl -s https://registry.npmjs.org/<pkg>/<version>    # dist.integrity
  curl -sL https://registry.npmjs.org/<pkg>/-/<pkg>-<version>.tgz

  moment/moment.min.js          moment@2.30.1, min/moment.min.js
                                (served as /assets/moment.min.js)
  moment/moment-timezone-with-data-10-year-range.min.js
                                moment-timezone@0.6.3,
                                builds/moment-timezone-with-data-10-year-range.min.js
  moment/moment-LICENSE         moment@2.30.1, LICENSE (MIT)
  moment/moment-timezone-LICENSE
                                moment-timezone@0.6.3, LICENSE (MIT)

moment and moment-timezone are the versions frontend/discourse/package.json
pins, and the timezone build is the one load-moment.js imports (the
10-year range). Both are byte-identical to the reference's node_modules.

  moment/locale/*.js            moment@2.30.1, locale/* (all 137; embedded
                                by build.rs, served in configureMoment's
                                script at /assets/moment-locale/<locale>.js,
                                src/moment_locale.rs)
  moment-timezone-names/*.js    @discourse/moment-timezone-names-translations@1.0.0,
                                locales/* (all 37, likewise)
  moment-timezone-names/LICENSE @discourse/moment-timezone-names-translations@1.0.0,
                                LICENSE (MIT)
  pikaday/pikaday.js            pikaday@1.8.2, pikaday.js with Discourse's
                                patches/pikaday.patch applied (its CommonJS
                                branch takes window.moment; the plain script
                                load this port does uses the global branch,
                                which the patch leaves alone)
  pikaday/LICENSE               pikaday@1.8.2, LICENSE (BSD-3-Clause and MIT)

The three tarballs were checked against their npm integrity (sha512); the
locale files are byte-identical to the tarballs and to the reference's
node_modules, pikaday.js to the reference's (the tarball's but for the
patch).

  chart.umd.min.js              chart.js@4.5.1, dist/chart.umd.min.js
  chart.js-LICENSE.md           chart.js@4.5.1, LICENSE.md (MIT)
  chartjs-adapter-moment.min.js chartjs-adapter-moment@1.0.1,
                                dist/chartjs-adapter-moment.min.js
  chartjs-adapter-moment-LICENSE.md
                                chartjs-adapter-moment@1.0.1, LICENSE.md (MIT)

Chart.js and its moment adapter are the versions frontend/discourse
pins and its chart-js-bundle (static/chart-js-bundle.js) imports for the
admin dashboard's charts, checked against the tarballs' npm integrity and
byte-identical to the reference's node_modules. The adapter is a UMD
script that reads window.moment and window.Chart, so both load before it.

  admin.css   Discourse's admin stylesheet as Rails compiles it at the
              vendored commit (app/assets/stylesheets/admin.scss, served
              as /stylesheets/admin_<digest>.css to staff), less its byte
              order mark and source map comment. It is fetched from the
              reference rather than ported rule by rule: it styles only the
              admin pages, which take it whole. To update, fetch the
              admin_<digest>.css a reference page links and strip the same
              two things.

  wizard.css  Discourse's wizard stylesheet as Rails compiles it at the
              vendored commit (app/assets/stylesheets/wizard.scss, served
              as /stylesheets/wizard_<digest>.css on the finish
              installation page), up to the fonts Stylesheet::Importer
              appends (from `.body-font-arial`), which the port serves as
              /assets/wizard_fonts.css, and less its source map comment.
              Fetched the same way as admin.css.

  discourse-solved-admin.css  discourse-solved's admin stylesheet as Rails
              compiles it (its `:admin` assets, dashboard-support.scss and
              report-related-items.scss, served as
              /stylesheets/discourse-solved_admin_<digest>.css to staff),
              less its source map comment; fetched the same way.

  ace/*.js      ace-builds@1.44.0, src-min-noconflict/: ace.js,
                mode-{scss,html,yaml,sql,javascript,text}.js,
                theme-{chaos,chrome}.js, ext-searchbox.js (served
                concatenated as /assets/ace-editor-bundle.js)
  ace/LICENSE   ace-builds@1.44.0, LICENSE (BSD-3-Clause)

Ace is the version frontend/discourse/package.json resolves (^1.44.0 in
the reference's node_modules), the files its ace-editor-bundle
(static/ace-editor-bundle.js) imports, in the minified noconflict build;
checked against the tarball's npm integrity (sha512), ace.js
byte-identical to the reference's node_modules.

  discourse-math-bundle/{mathjax,katex}/
                discourse_math_bundle gem 1.0.1 (the version the
                reference's bundle installs for plugins/discourse-math),
                vendor/assets/mathjax (MathJax 4.1.0) and
                vendor/assets/katex (KaTeX 0.16.27), all 247 files
                verbatim (embedded by build.rs, served at
                /plugins/discourse-math/1.0.1/{mathjax,katex}/...,
                src/plugins/math.rs)

The gem ships no license files; MathJax is Apache-2.0 and KaTeX MIT.
Copied from an installed gem and compared with `diff -r`. To update,
install the new gem version, replace both trees and bump
BUNDLE_VERSION and the route in src/routes/mod.rs.
